1
00:02:04,463 --> 00:02:08,463
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE FILMING
OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:12,802 --> 00:02:23,752
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:03:02,261 --> 00:03:03,621
It's really him!

4
00:03:05,456 --> 00:03:07,316
Oh my Allah, it's surely him!

5
00:03:47,251 --> 00:03:48,801
While walking in darkness...

6
00:03:50,610 --> 00:03:51,970
without my shadow...

7
00:03:53,373 --> 00:03:55,053
I killed my enemies...

8
00:03:56,017 --> 00:03:57,447
and lost my friends.

9
00:04:00,069 --> 00:04:04,069
My ancestors' shrines were destroyed.

10
00:04:06,575 --> 00:04:08,365
After I shouted for freedom...

11
00:04:09,159 --> 00:04:10,539
I lost my voice.

12
00:04:12,129 --> 00:04:13,739
I have so many troubles.

13
00:04:15,128 --> 00:04:16,988
I am not only surrounded by ambushes...

14
00:04:17,648 --> 00:04:18,878
but also betrayals.

15
00:04:21,153 --> 00:04:22,243
My heart aches...

16
00:04:24,073 --> 00:04:25,183
as well as my being.

17
00:05:44,270 --> 00:05:46,620
The imminent draws near, Osman.

18
00:05:48,286 --> 00:05:50,196
The persecution is about come to an end.

19
00:05:50,636 --> 00:05:52,886
Time will give us a new resurrection.

20
00:05:54,041 --> 00:05:55,691
As long as you do not fall asleep.

21
00:05:56,711 --> 00:05:58,851
As long as you do not fall asleep, my son!

22
00:06:00,828 --> 00:06:04,418
Kin of Oghuz only go through bad incidents
when they are asleep.

23
00:06:08,384 --> 00:06:09,644
Wake up, my son!

24
00:06:10,897 --> 00:06:11,917
Rise! My Son!

25
00:06:14,438 --> 00:06:15,478
Rise! My Son!

26
00:06:16,830 --> 00:06:20,070
''Kin of Oghuz only go through bad
incidents when they are asleep.''

27
00:06:30,163 --> 00:06:32,033
My mighty, grandfather!

28
00:08:22,934 --> 00:08:23,934
Holy Yama!

29
00:08:24,516 --> 00:08:27,866
The pain and torture...

30
00:08:27,866 --> 00:08:31,866
I served to Osman and his family.

31
00:08:31,866 --> 00:08:33,336
Are only for you.

32
00:08:34,162 --> 00:08:37,332
Death is only for you.

33
00:08:40,997 --> 00:08:44,068
All these plunders and booties are for
you.

34
00:08:48,345 --> 00:08:52,345
From your iron and muddy castle...

35
00:08:53,514 --> 00:08:56,844
Hear the voice of Balgay!

36
00:08:58,136 --> 00:09:02,136
Accept this present from Balgay!

37
00:09:38,748 --> 00:09:41,898
Ever since I started to serve Genghis
Khan...

38
00:09:43,492 --> 00:09:45,432
All the blood I shed...

39
00:09:47,663 --> 00:09:49,863
Gave pleasure to your mighty castle!

40
00:10:04,508 --> 00:10:07,348
The tears of those I sacrificed...

41
00:10:07,369 --> 00:10:09,579
had reached to Doymadım River...

42
00:10:10,589 --> 00:10:13,429
then gave glory to our spirits.

43
00:10:15,361 --> 00:10:17,641
As well as reputation.

44
00:10:23,768 --> 00:10:24,658
Now...

45
00:10:26,766 --> 00:10:27,746
I serve you...

46
00:10:29,186 --> 00:10:30,896
Osman!

47
00:10:34,969 --> 00:10:37,989
For Erluk Khan!

48
00:11:21,961 --> 00:11:22,961
Rise, my son!

49
00:12:02,069 --> 00:12:03,349
Osman.

50
00:12:09,374 --> 00:12:10,444
What's wrong, brother?

51
00:12:12,277 --> 00:12:14,057
I hope nothing is wrong, brother.

52
00:12:14,635 --> 00:12:15,735
A dream within a dream.

53
00:12:16,167 --> 00:12:17,607
A trick within a trick.

54
00:12:20,681 --> 00:12:21,921
My Bey, we are ready.

55
00:12:22,338 --> 00:12:24,348
With your permission, we can leave.

56
00:12:24,601 --> 00:12:26,451
I don't want any mistakes.

57
00:12:27,041 --> 00:12:30,031
We gave such a deposit to Balgay to claim
our Tent back...

58
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:33,270
that now it's time we take it back.

59
00:12:34,542 --> 00:12:38,002
Now we will teach those Mongol dogs what
it means to lose.

60
00:12:38,777 --> 00:12:41,807
Balgay will drown in his own dreams.

61
00:12:42,130 --> 00:12:42,990
If Allah permits.

62
00:12:43,903 --> 00:12:46,393
We will become the worst dreams of
Heathens.

63
00:12:47,210 --> 00:12:51,210
We must howl like wolves and set the
biggest ambush ever for those tyrants.

64
00:12:51,478 --> 00:12:54,448
We must be as sharp as Zulfiqar and bring
peace upon this land.

65
00:12:54,702 --> 00:12:55,402
Let's go!

66
00:12:55,648 --> 00:12:56,388
Oh, Allah!

67
00:12:57,671 --> 00:12:58,371
Let's go!

68
00:13:03,829 --> 00:13:04,559
Let's go!

69
00:13:06,616 --> 00:13:08,116
May Allah help us!

70
00:13:08,130 --> 00:13:09,170
May Allah be with us!

71
00:13:51,056 --> 00:13:52,506
We are almost ready.

72
00:13:53,558 --> 00:13:55,718
Do you want anything else, Balgay?

73
00:13:56,486 --> 00:13:59,756
I only want the mighty Beys of Mongols...

74
00:13:59,756 --> 00:14:05,011
to see who is holding the holy agenda of
almighty Genghis Khan...

75
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:08,541
And who the true monarch is...

76
00:14:08,541 --> 00:14:12,981
so that they bow in front of Balgay!

77
00:14:13,989 --> 00:14:16,879
Geyhatu will be so angry when he hears
the Beys bow to you...

78
00:14:16,879 --> 00:14:19,919
and that you hold the holy agendas.

79
00:14:20,825 --> 00:14:22,805
They will become your enemies, Balgay.

80
00:14:24,857 --> 00:14:29,477
Those who become the enemies of Balgay
should look for strong allies, Cerkutay.

81
00:14:34,443 --> 00:14:36,013
I am the new monarch.

82
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:42,000
And those are the commanders
of my army.

83
00:14:42,561 --> 00:14:46,561
Soon, in Constantinople, our language will
be spoken!

84
00:14:49,757 --> 00:14:51,347
Nothing besides this matters.

85
00:17:09,794 --> 00:17:11,414
Kayıs are the first ones to beg.

86
00:17:13,044 --> 00:17:16,294
A Hatun without a man is
like an infertile soil.

87
00:17:17,934 --> 00:17:19,564
Imbecile Dündar.

88
00:17:38,055 --> 00:17:39,335
Walk!

89
00:18:06,686 --> 00:18:08,526
How is the situation in Söğüt, Erkut?

90
00:18:08,643 --> 00:18:09,973
Balgay has left Söğüt.

91
00:18:10,191 --> 00:18:12,761
They say he moved his Tent to
somewhere hidden.

92
00:18:14,779 --> 00:18:19,019
No one can have their own Tents on
these soils except my father!

93
00:18:19,447 --> 00:18:23,447
Those who attempt this shall die next to
their tents.

94
00:18:24,334 --> 00:18:26,794
They bullied the merchants of
our Bazaar my Bey.

95
00:18:26,843 --> 00:18:28,993
They took their goods and assaulted them.

96
00:18:29,279 --> 00:18:30,869
What do they aim by that?

97
00:18:31,059 --> 00:18:32,839
They want to bring food to Balgay.

98
00:18:32,839 --> 00:18:34,799
Head Beys of Mongols are on their way.

99
00:18:34,799 --> 00:18:36,939
And Balgay will have a feast tonight.

100
00:18:39,741 --> 00:18:43,411
Those thieves will show us Balgay's
location.

101
00:18:43,586 --> 00:18:45,116
Do you understand, my Konur?

102
00:18:45,172 --> 00:18:46,982
As you wish, my Bey!

103
00:18:47,679 --> 00:18:49,915
I will rip their lungs and present them to
you!

104
00:18:49,915 --> 00:18:51,725
You should be all careful!

105
00:18:52,759 --> 00:18:54,409
Let's go now!

106
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,280
Why is the Hatun of Kayıs...

107
00:20:09,630 --> 00:20:11,060
bows in front of me.

108
00:20:12,056 --> 00:20:13,386
Mighty Balgay!

109
00:20:15,885 --> 00:20:17,755
I have some words to tell you.

110
00:20:18,808 --> 00:20:19,938
Tell me already...

111
00:20:21,653 --> 00:20:25,353
But be careful, you will understand the
death which comes from Balgay...

112
00:20:25,912 --> 00:20:28,932
only when your spirit meets with sky.

113
00:20:30,652 --> 00:20:32,102
I came here for my son.

114
00:20:33,244 --> 00:20:34,624
He has left the Tent.

115
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:39,380
You are my only hope.

116
00:20:45,737 --> 00:20:47,117
Why should I care...

117
00:20:47,617 --> 00:20:48,827
about your son?

118
00:20:49,742 --> 00:20:51,692
My son is with Osman at the moment.

119
00:20:53,295 --> 00:20:55,675
He clashes next to Osman.

120
00:20:59,359 --> 00:21:01,489
You say don't drink my son's blood...

121
00:21:02,574 --> 00:21:04,024
don't drill his lungs...

122
00:21:05,826 --> 00:21:08,696
don't feed the birds and wolves with his
head.

123
00:21:13,836 --> 00:21:15,736
What do you offer in exchange?

124
00:21:16,719 --> 00:21:17,559
Osman...

125
00:21:18,182 --> 00:21:18,892
and...

126
00:21:20,326 --> 00:21:21,116
Edebali.

127
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:48,770
So you came here with promises.

128
00:22:26,701 --> 00:22:28,861
In exchange for what I desire...

129
00:22:30,222 --> 00:22:32,202
you want to reunite with your son.

130
00:22:34,549 --> 00:22:37,309
The person who doesn't think before
promising something...

131
00:22:37,329 --> 00:22:38,789
must not cry...

132
00:22:39,538 --> 00:22:41,708
when she fails to fulfill what she
promised.

133
00:22:45,836 --> 00:22:47,216
You are a smart woman.

134
00:22:50,933 --> 00:22:53,033
You exactly know who to obey.

135
00:22:54,434 --> 00:22:56,754
My power stands with you.

136
00:22:58,114 --> 00:22:59,213
Now, leave.

137
00:22:59,223 --> 00:23:01,473
Then report me the information you
promised.

138
00:23:03,280 --> 00:23:05,410
If you do something wrong...

139
00:23:05,581 --> 00:23:09,581
I will separate Batur's flesh
from his bones.

140
00:23:10,752 --> 00:23:12,612
Then, feed my dogs with him.

141
00:23:14,327 --> 00:23:15,707
Don't you worry.

142
00:23:18,119 --> 00:23:20,629
Zöhre will be loyal to you.

143
00:23:30,245 --> 00:23:32,385
The number of dogs I control increases.

144
00:23:34,983 --> 00:23:36,413
Give the word immediately.

145
00:23:36,771 --> 00:23:38,461
Bring her husband here.

146
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:40,650
Dündar deserves a present now.

147
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:12,516
Where is your mother, my daughter?

148
00:24:12,681 --> 00:24:15,121
She said she will leave to pick up medical
herbals.

149
00:24:16,010 --> 00:24:18,030
Couldn't she find a better time?

150
00:24:19,093 --> 00:24:20,453
Father, you know my mother.

151
00:24:21,295 --> 00:24:22,855
She can't keep her mouth shut.

152
00:24:23,629 --> 00:24:25,629
If she can't share her problems with us...

153
00:24:25,629 --> 00:24:27,789
she will try to talk about them with
flowers.

154
00:24:28,429 --> 00:24:30,229
Herbals are only her excuses.

155
00:24:30,310 --> 00:24:32,830
What is it that problem she can't talk
about with us?

156
00:24:32,830 --> 00:24:35,490
You have been wearing down my mother
lately, father.

157
00:24:38,226 --> 00:24:39,926
Don't worry, my daughter.

158
00:24:39,926 --> 00:24:42,396
Your mother always knew what she did.

159
00:24:42,468 --> 00:24:45,238
She isn't anything like those herbals she
collects.

160
00:24:46,352 --> 00:24:47,462
Don't say that.

161
00:24:48,451 --> 00:24:50,171
You broke her heart so much.

162
00:24:51,768 --> 00:24:55,108
I heard you asked for the presence of
Hazal Hatun and brother Bahadır.

163
00:24:56,458 --> 00:24:58,598
How could you forget what happened
so quickly?

164
00:24:58,698 --> 00:25:02,585
Dinner table of a Bey should be as wide
as his Tent, my daughter.

165
00:25:04,313 --> 00:25:07,633
A person who knows how to act will not be
troubled with such matters.

166
00:25:09,176 --> 00:25:12,696
You should finish your dinner, not be
overwhelmed with these.

167
00:25:13,585 --> 00:25:14,395
Come on.

168
00:25:14,582 --> 00:25:16,072
Do you think it is easy?

169
00:25:16,794 --> 00:25:18,964
One of my brothers is on the road...

170
00:25:18,964 --> 00:25:21,524
while there is no news from Batur brother.

171
00:25:21,770 --> 00:25:23,160
May I come in, uncle?

172
00:25:23,742 --> 00:25:25,402
You may come in, Gündüz.

173
00:25:36,140 --> 00:25:37,590
You demanded my presence, uncle.

174
00:25:37,590 --> 00:25:38,400
Come.

175
00:25:38,840 --> 00:25:39,790
Sit.

176
00:25:44,598 --> 00:25:46,638
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.

177
00:25:48,824 --> 00:25:50,124
Be my guest.

178
00:25:50,993 --> 00:25:52,363
Thank you, uncle.

179
00:25:57,057 --> 00:25:59,347
The situation of our Tent is
obvious, nephew.

180
00:26:00,951 --> 00:26:01,811
Mongols...

181
00:26:02,481 --> 00:26:05,241
destroyed everything along with
our people.

182
00:26:06,668 --> 00:26:09,488
I want you to leave for Nicaea.

183
00:26:11,457 --> 00:26:13,807
The Bazaar is very fertile there.

184
00:26:14,016 --> 00:26:18,636
You need to sell everything we have
without any questions.

185
00:26:21,980 --> 00:26:22,690
Uncle.

186
00:26:27,059 --> 00:26:29,009
If that's what you want, I will go there.

187
00:26:29,995 --> 00:26:30,765
Osman?

188
00:26:32,248 --> 00:26:34,498
What's going to happen to Osman?

189
00:26:39,381 --> 00:26:43,381
Osman is being punished by his
youthfulness right now.

190
00:26:44,725 --> 00:26:48,725
He will learn from his lessons day by day.

191
00:26:48,822 --> 00:26:50,432
Don't worry, my nephew.

192
00:26:51,498 --> 00:26:53,288
I prepared such a great plan that...

193
00:26:54,734 --> 00:26:57,614
in the end, everyone will get what they
want.

194
00:26:58,527 --> 00:27:02,527
Also, I will hug him as soon as he comes
back...

195
00:27:03,236 --> 00:27:04,856
and gain his heart again.

196
00:27:07,169 --> 00:27:08,479
As you say, uncle.

197
00:27:08,699 --> 00:27:09,629
Don't worry.

198
00:27:10,731 --> 00:27:14,731
I will leave as soon as I can.

199
00:27:34,883 --> 00:27:37,933
Tell the Tent guarding Alps to move into
forest.

200
00:27:38,798 --> 00:27:41,763
They should defend this position in case
of a sneak attack.

201
00:27:41,763 --> 00:27:42,993
Understood, our Bey!

202
00:27:47,958 --> 00:27:49,918
My Bey, Bamsı Bey has arrived.

203
00:27:51,468 --> 00:27:52,258
Let him come in.

204
00:28:08,162 --> 00:28:10,596
What made you come all the way
to here, Bamsı Bey?

205
00:28:10,596 --> 00:28:12,976
I didn't think you would know the road
to our Tent.

206
00:28:15,081 --> 00:28:18,011
When I first came to these lands, there
were no ways at all.

207
00:28:22,545 --> 00:28:25,195
Neither time nor the location is the same.
Bamsi Bey.

208
00:28:25,315 --> 00:28:27,537
The youth started to riot against their
Beys.

209
00:28:27,898 --> 00:28:30,208
I came here because of the exact problem.

210
00:28:30,437 --> 00:28:33,587
I heard the wild winds started a breeze
between two high mountains.

211
00:28:33,587 --> 00:28:35,788
I couldn't believe when I heard the
incident.

212
00:28:36,435 --> 00:28:37,995
Now, tell me.

213
00:28:38,071 --> 00:28:39,291
What happened?

214
00:28:47,475 --> 00:28:50,255
Kill me right here, right now. Osman.

215
00:28:51,303 --> 00:28:53,053
Or else I will find you.

216
00:28:54,867 --> 00:28:55,897
Kill me!

217
00:29:04,958 --> 00:29:07,228
Don't you ever dare to be on my path
again.

218
00:29:14,277 --> 00:29:17,097
Eventually, those we praised proved
themselves unworthy...

219
00:29:17,097 --> 00:29:19,617
and they wanted to go on their
own way, Bamsı Bey.

220
00:29:20,464 --> 00:29:23,584
Do you hear what you are telling me right
now?

221
00:29:23,648 --> 00:29:26,938
There are sometimes sad incidents like
this between comrades like us.

222
00:29:26,938 --> 00:29:29,138
But, only for the sake of our path.

223
00:29:29,138 --> 00:29:31,918
Osman has fallen both from my eyes and
my heart, Bamsı Bey.

224
00:29:34,619 --> 00:29:37,529
You are two Valiants of Kayıs.

225
00:29:38,378 --> 00:29:40,888
This is not how you are supposed to act.

226
00:29:40,888 --> 00:29:42,518
You are brothers in arms!

227
00:29:42,518 --> 00:29:44,238
If we are brothers in arms...

228
00:29:44,238 --> 00:29:46,648
Why did he keep the agendas as a secret?

229
00:29:47,364 --> 00:29:49,344
Ertuğrul Bey also had secrets.

230
00:29:49,624 --> 00:29:51,614
But we weren't offended at all.

231
00:29:54,093 --> 00:29:54,913
Dündar...

232
00:29:54,913 --> 00:29:57,353
sent him to exile after he learned about
it.

233
00:29:58,554 --> 00:30:00,364
Why didn't you say anything back then?

234
00:30:00,364 --> 00:30:01,644
Dündar is our Bey.

235
00:30:01,644 --> 00:30:03,454
We can't question his orders.

236
00:30:03,481 --> 00:30:04,881
Yeah, Dündar Bey.

237
00:30:07,290 --> 00:30:08,840
This is the Tent he rules.

238
00:30:09,693 --> 00:30:11,313
This is the throne.

239
00:30:11,947 --> 00:30:14,677
Aren't we as important as
our Bey Dündar, Bamsı Bey?

240
00:30:15,005 --> 00:30:19,045
A Bey doesn't hesitate when he gives the
commands!

241
00:30:20,194 --> 00:30:23,044
A Bey always knows his place when he
confronts a mistake!

242
00:30:24,088 --> 00:30:27,428
A Bey always tries to come up with
solutions instead of running away!

243
00:30:35,338 --> 00:30:37,458
This spear doesn't fit its sack, Bamsı
Bey.

244
00:30:38,898 --> 00:30:40,378
From now on, Osman is my enemy.

245
00:30:40,378 --> 00:30:41,308
Nothing else.

246
00:30:43,615 --> 00:30:46,965
Don't stand between us so that no blood
will be spilled onto you.

247
00:30:50,840 --> 00:30:52,910
You are newbie Valiant.

248
00:30:53,649 --> 00:30:55,149
Right now...

249
00:30:55,238 --> 00:30:57,988
you are the Bey of the Tent your father
left you.

250
00:30:59,319 --> 00:31:00,749
But there is one thing...

251
00:31:01,541 --> 00:31:04,241
they either didn't teach you well...

252
00:31:04,241 --> 00:31:06,531
or you didn't understand it well enough.

253
00:31:06,531 --> 00:31:07,281
Samsa.

254
00:31:09,412 --> 00:31:10,452
I...

255
00:31:11,753 --> 00:31:14,373
am the right hand of Ertuğrul Ghazi...

256
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:15,783
mighty Bamsı Beyrek.

257
00:31:16,563 --> 00:31:18,863
I whet my sword with blood...

258
00:31:19,705 --> 00:31:22,455
and live side by side with my fate.

259
00:31:24,916 --> 00:31:27,266
As you elder, I give preaches to you.

260
00:31:27,639 --> 00:31:29,479
But you try to darken upon us.

261
00:31:31,550 --> 00:31:33,890
If you continue with this stubbornness...

262
00:31:33,890 --> 00:31:35,840
you will be alone more than ever.

263
00:31:39,103 --> 00:31:40,823
Wolves howl at our naiveness...

264
00:31:40,829 --> 00:31:42,869
while the birds make fun of them.

265
00:31:43,691 --> 00:31:46,191
Loneliness is my destiny, Bamsı Bey.

266
00:31:49,357 --> 00:31:51,307
You spent so much effort on us...

267
00:31:51,844 --> 00:31:53,844
but this has nothing to do with you.

268
00:31:55,194 --> 00:31:57,133
If you disagree, the door is there.

269
00:32:05,275 --> 00:32:06,995
All the effort I spent you...

270
00:32:08,242 --> 00:32:09,692
all the effort I spent...

271
00:32:09,692 --> 00:32:11,022
I feel sad for them.

272
00:32:12,713 --> 00:32:13,443
You...

273
00:32:14,323 --> 00:32:16,083
have become presumptuous.

274
00:32:16,769 --> 00:32:18,769
You forgot about our moral laws.

275
00:32:19,813 --> 00:32:22,003
Evil has set a tent inside your spirit.

276
00:32:23,485 --> 00:32:24,385
Now...

277
00:32:25,315 --> 00:32:28,285
you'll either destroy his tent and get rid
of the Devil...

278
00:32:28,459 --> 00:32:30,989
or nobody can save you from me.

279
00:32:33,053 --> 00:32:35,893
I'll give you some time to think...

280
00:32:36,814 --> 00:32:39,344
If I see that Devil in your spirit
again...

281
00:32:40,789 --> 00:32:43,439
I will destroy this Tent upon you.

282
00:32:45,303 --> 00:32:47,733
I will destroy this Tent upon you, Samsa.

283
00:33:08,044 --> 00:33:09,834
Please stop.

284
00:33:10,949 --> 00:33:12,039
Don't do it.

285
00:33:12,990 --> 00:33:14,010
Leave us alone.

286
00:33:47,442 --> 00:33:48,182
Go there!

287
00:33:49,227 --> 00:33:50,617
I beg you, please stop.

288
00:33:50,977 --> 00:33:52,403
You took everything I have.

289
00:33:52,613 --> 00:33:53,613
Enough already.

290
00:33:54,133 --> 00:33:55,983
At least give my horses back.

291
00:36:33,045 --> 00:36:35,525
Balgay is waiting for you, Dündar Bey.

292
00:36:35,525 --> 00:36:37,585
Do you know what he demands from me?

293
00:36:39,629 --> 00:36:43,629
Balgay doesn't demand, he takes,
Dündar Bey.

294
00:36:47,833 --> 00:36:49,773
He just takes.

295
00:37:44,407 --> 00:37:46,367
Stop! Stop!

296
00:39:02,052 --> 00:39:06,342
Hang their bodies to the side of the road.
Those who pass by shall see them.

297
00:39:06,734 --> 00:39:10,334
So that this fear of the Mongols perishes.

298
00:39:10,519 --> 00:39:15,589
They should see that Osman and his Alps
have rekindled the fire of resurrection.

299
00:39:19,810 --> 00:39:23,040
Let's go. We have a long night ahead.

300
00:39:57,784 --> 00:40:01,954
In the name of Kayı Tent, I've come to
inform you that...

301
00:40:01,954 --> 00:40:04,024
... we've accepted your
leadership, Balgay.

302
00:40:06,998 --> 00:40:11,708
Blessed commander, almighty Balgay.

303
00:40:15,851 --> 00:40:17,821
Balgay likes you.

304
00:40:19,540 --> 00:40:22,700
You've started to come to reason, Dündar.

305
00:40:24,146 --> 00:40:26,546
And you exiled Osman.

306
00:40:26,715 --> 00:40:33,895
From now on, those who might hurt our
loyalty to you can't populate Kayı Tent.

307
00:40:34,575 --> 00:40:41,815
More loyal you are to Balgay,
more graceful he will be.

308
00:40:43,561 --> 00:40:48,641
Your brother Ertuğrul was generous and
made you...

309
00:40:48,641 --> 00:40:50,951
... the alternate Bey of the Kayı Tent.

310
00:40:51,885 --> 00:40:56,355
Now I will be like a father to you.
Stand up.

311
00:41:05,940 --> 00:41:12,920
From now on you are, not the alternate,
but the noble Bey of the Kayı Tent.

312
00:41:34,197 --> 00:41:37,427
These golds are my gift to you.

313
00:41:44,414 --> 00:41:47,464
Spend them, or hand them out as you wish.

314
00:41:52,799 --> 00:41:58,889
How could that be? Kayı Tent's throne is
my brother's.

315
00:41:59,952 --> 00:42:02,032
Beys won't accept this.

316
00:42:03,286 --> 00:42:06,386
Don't worry, Dündar.

317
00:42:07,034 --> 00:42:09,804
Easy there, Dündar.

318
00:42:11,095 --> 00:42:20,575
Balgay is very generous. I also grant you
the Bannerlordship which all Beys follow.

319
00:42:42,538 --> 00:42:49,958
Now go and fly this mighty symbol
in the Kayı Tent.

320
00:42:50,590 --> 00:42:55,460
So that everyone knows
the Mongols' power...

321
00:42:55,460 --> 00:43:00,230
... who swear on ruling every place
where the sun rises and sets.

322
00:43:09,948 --> 00:43:12,838
Why me, Balgay?

323
00:43:13,276 --> 00:43:19,066
Is there and other Bey
as brave as you, Dündar Bey?

324
00:43:44,784 --> 00:43:50,814
Kayı Tent will always be grateful for you.

325
00:43:50,814 --> 00:43:56,334
No need for empty words. I have
other guests. You may leave.

326
00:44:15,883 --> 00:44:19,883
Bring me the laws and the guardian dagger.

327
00:45:56,077 --> 00:45:58,487
Do you see what I see, my Bey?

328
00:45:59,375 --> 00:46:02,065
I wish I was blind, Konur.

329
00:46:12,494 --> 00:46:16,894
He offers his flesh to the dog
who attacked our Tent.

330
00:46:19,066 --> 00:46:23,846
He begged Balgay so much that
his tongue wrinkled.

331
00:46:24,436 --> 00:46:27,556
He kneeled so much that
his knees started to decay.

332
00:46:56,231 --> 00:46:59,521
He rides his horse as if he won a victory.

333
00:47:03,177 --> 00:47:06,147
What do you think he's doing in that
dog's Tent, my Bey?

334
00:47:08,777 --> 00:47:11,757
My father's throne was the only thing
he didn't sell.

335
00:47:11,757 --> 00:47:14,577
My Bey, do you think he's bold
enough to do this?

336
00:47:58,437 --> 00:47:59,957
Move!

337
00:48:20,444 --> 00:48:23,184
Our ancestor Genghis...

338
00:48:23,869 --> 00:48:30,109
... descends from the blue wolf who lives
in the Burkhan Khaldun mountains.

339
00:48:36,447 --> 00:48:43,017
I'll paint my face just blue.

340
00:49:10,504 --> 00:49:15,034
I'll carry this dagger which is
a reminiscence from...

341
00:49:15,034 --> 00:49:18,530
... our ancestor Genghis with honour

342
00:50:10,645 --> 00:50:15,605
Don't turn your face away, Selcan Hatun.
Don't increase my troubles.

343
00:50:15,605 --> 00:50:18,925
If you had yourself together, you'd not
have such big troubles.

344
00:50:19,145 --> 00:50:21,365
If I made mistakes, it's because
I was scared.

345
00:50:21,717 --> 00:50:25,817
My fears have come true. My valiant son
went away.

346
00:50:27,040 --> 00:50:29,560
Come with me, Selcan Hatun.

347
00:50:32,188 --> 00:50:34,278
I have things to tell you.

348
00:50:35,259 --> 00:50:36,919
Important things.

349
00:50:45,655 --> 00:50:48,755
I don't have much time.
Say whatever you want to say.

350
00:50:49,127 --> 00:50:54,437
A child causes sorrow a thousand times
more to the mother.

351
00:50:55,155 --> 00:50:57,635
You'll understand this.

352
00:50:58,657 --> 00:51:02,657
- Take this fardel.
- What is this?

353
00:51:02,790 --> 00:51:04,490
To my Batur.

354
00:51:04,854 --> 00:51:10,394
I don't know where he is.
You're in touch with Osman.

355
00:51:11,326 --> 00:51:14,026
You'll definitely hear
something about him.

356
00:51:14,842 --> 00:51:18,672
They shall give it to my Batur.
Clean clothes for him.

357
00:51:18,672 --> 00:51:21,372
- Zöhre!
- Don't, Selcan Hatun!

358
00:51:23,187 --> 00:51:25,727
I know what you are going to say.

359
00:51:26,017 --> 00:51:29,387
But your words don't heal my wounds.

360
00:51:30,034 --> 00:51:32,834
Dündar Bey disowned Batur.

361
00:51:33,511 --> 00:51:38,111
Worse, he told Bahadır to bring
his mother with him.

362
00:51:38,627 --> 00:51:40,747
What are you talking about, Zöhre?

363
00:51:41,172 --> 00:51:43,772
Are Bahadır and his mother coming here?

364
00:51:45,313 --> 00:51:49,673
- We're doomed.
- I'm begging you, Selcan Hatun.

365
00:51:49,673 --> 00:51:52,313
Make this fardel reach my Batur.

366
00:51:53,745 --> 00:51:55,865
About Osman...

367
00:51:56,738 --> 00:52:02,938
I understand. I understand him and
why Batur went with him.

368
00:52:05,888 --> 00:52:07,508
I agree with him.

369
00:52:07,793 --> 00:52:12,373
If you hear something about Osman.
Tell me.

370
00:52:14,011 --> 00:52:16,551
Knowing that they are doing okay
is enough.

371
00:52:25,906 --> 00:52:29,076
I hope Osman doesn't do
something crazy, brother.

372
00:52:30,415 --> 00:52:33,325
How can you call someone who's not crazy
a Bey, brother?

373
00:52:33,437 --> 00:52:38,517
Didn't we stay quiet in the meeting so he
could tear his heart out?

374
00:52:40,205 --> 00:52:46,975
Those who don't suffer can't be Beys.

375
00:52:47,562 --> 00:52:52,035
He'll suffer greatly so that
he can be the hope...

376
00:52:52,035 --> 00:52:56,445
... of these people in the
future, brother.

377
00:53:01,338 --> 00:53:05,148
Thank you, you're right, Bamsı brother.

378
00:53:06,257 --> 00:53:11,317
My heart will be torn apart if something
bad happens to Osman.

379
00:53:46,743 --> 00:53:50,433
Bamsı! Brother!

380
00:53:51,306 --> 00:53:53,776
Do you see what I'm seeing?

381
00:53:58,588 --> 00:54:06,648
Abdurrahman brother! These eyes witnessed
such betrayals...

382
00:54:08,235 --> 00:54:11,735
... but they never saw
something like this.

383
00:54:11,998 --> 00:54:15,998
I never saw or heard something like this.

384
00:54:22,297 --> 00:54:24,327
What are we going to do now?

385
00:54:35,003 --> 00:54:37,693
Long live Dündar Bey!

386
00:56:19,489 --> 00:56:29,449
Kayı's valiant Beys, valiant Alps,
and community.

387
00:56:32,080 --> 00:56:38,010
I'm flying another flag beside
the blessed flag of Kayı...

388
00:56:38,010 --> 00:56:43,700
... worthy of my ancestor Oghuz, my father
Süleyman Şah

389
00:56:45,873 --> 00:56:51,083
I wanted you to know and be proud.

390
00:56:51,492 --> 00:56:58,082
I did another great thing for these lands
my brother Ertuğrul Bey conquered.

391
00:57:00,227 --> 00:57:06,267
I was blessed with, with my Allah's
permission, the Bannerlordship.

392
00:57:07,429 --> 00:57:13,339
Because of this, Kayıs are
full of hope once again!

393
00:57:14,368 --> 00:57:20,548
Long live Dündar Bey!
Long live Dündar Bey!

394
00:57:30,416 --> 00:57:36,826
With me being the Bannerlord,
in these lands or in our Tent...

395
00:57:36,826 --> 00:57:42,266
... we've come to the end of living
without leaders.

396
00:57:43,265 --> 00:57:48,115
We'll work more, we'll strive more!

397
00:57:48,336 --> 00:57:57,756
You traitor! I hope Osman comes here
and destroys your fake magnificence!

398
00:57:59,720 --> 00:58:03,720
Selcan Hatun wait! Not now. Not now.

399
00:58:09,934 --> 00:58:16,494
As the Kayıs Bey and
the Bannerlord of these lands...

400
00:58:16,494 --> 00:58:20,924
... I'm waiting for my Tent's
Beys in my tent.

401
00:58:20,924 --> 00:58:30,444
Just like me, their duties
and responsibilities also increased.

402
00:58:32,431 --> 00:58:36,431
May Allah help you all.

403
00:58:37,040 --> 00:58:42,320
- Long live Dündar Bey!
- Long live Dündar Bey!

404
00:59:12,863 --> 00:59:16,863
Genghis Khan's laws are in Balgay's tent.

405
00:59:22,966 --> 00:59:26,016
My Bey! This won't be easy.

406
00:59:26,976 --> 00:59:30,976
Balgay invited over a great Mongol
commander for tonight.

407
00:59:31,714 --> 00:59:36,394
He wants to be more powerful. He wants to
advance in the Mongol khanate.

408
00:59:36,827 --> 00:59:40,827
We'll crush his spirit.

409
00:59:41,061 --> 00:59:42,991
If Allah permits, my Bey.

410
00:59:47,628 --> 00:59:49,338
Let's go.

411
01:00:11,552 --> 01:00:19,242
Now I'm both the Bey of Kayı Tent
and the Bannerlord.

412
01:00:22,543 --> 01:00:25,773
Dark days are gone.

413
01:00:27,225 --> 01:00:30,795
Duty came with its blessings.

414
01:00:31,850 --> 01:00:33,750
Saltuk!

415
01:01:39,646 --> 01:01:47,096
We didn't say anything so you could
get the Tent together!

416
01:01:47,287 --> 01:01:51,137
But does being Mongols' friend mean?

417
01:01:53,285 --> 01:01:57,555
I made these decisions for Kayı's safety.

418
01:01:59,257 --> 01:02:05,017
Brothers! The Mongols
are way stronger than us!

419
01:02:05,207 --> 01:02:10,517
We're not strong enough to deal with them.
Don't you still understand?

420
01:02:12,057 --> 01:02:19,137
I want to have good senses
and protect our Tent from trouble.

421
01:02:20,479 --> 01:02:24,719
Why did you take the gold then?
Does freedom have a price?

422
01:02:25,325 --> 01:02:31,005
I've been assisting this Tent for years.
I've never seen such a thing!

423
01:02:32,412 --> 01:02:36,812
In Kayı, Beys choose the Bey.
Who chose you?

424
01:02:37,463 --> 01:02:40,203
Who put you in that throne, Dündar Bey?

425
01:02:41,641 --> 01:02:45,921
What was I supposed to do?
Cause another slaughter?

426
01:02:46,362 --> 01:02:50,632
Kayı's fortune was gained with blood!

427
01:02:51,164 --> 01:02:55,734
I wish they broke my neck so
I couldn't see you kneel, Dündar Bey!

428
01:02:55,734 --> 01:02:59,704
What was he supposed to do? Refuse the
duties and refuse to kneel?

429
01:03:00,718 --> 01:03:04,198
Let the Mongols decide the Tent's fate?

430
01:03:05,148 --> 01:03:09,278
We saw those who refused. Mr Blacksmith.

431
01:03:10,640 --> 01:03:14,640
They destroyed Kayı's dignity.

432
01:03:16,575 --> 01:03:20,255
They became Balgay's cattle.

433
01:03:20,255 --> 01:03:26,485
Şahin Bey! Revolting and
becoming cattle...

434
01:03:26,485 --> 01:03:29,495
... is better than kneeling and
being their dog!

435
01:03:29,495 --> 01:03:33,495
Enough! Watch your words,
Abdurrahman Gazi!

436
01:03:33,495 --> 01:03:38,695
No, Dündar Bey! No!
Abdurrahman Gazi is right!

437
01:03:39,583 --> 01:03:44,473
History of a battle also
includes the defeat.

438
01:03:45,063 --> 01:03:53,723
But it doesn't include the dishonour
that comes from taking your enemy's gold.

439
01:03:54,106 --> 01:04:03,126
Watch your words, Bamsı Beyrek!
Otherwise you won't be a Bey or an Alp!

440
01:04:05,126 --> 01:04:11,266
Dündar Bey! My hairs turned grey when
my son became a martyr!

441
01:04:12,624 --> 01:04:18,524
If we were going to kneel like this, why
did we let so many of us die?

442
01:04:19,388 --> 01:04:26,798
Dündar Bey! Enemy's oily foods have
seduced you out of your faith.

443
01:04:27,188 --> 01:04:32,838
But know this.
Every cloud has a silver lining.

444
01:04:52,951 --> 01:04:56,951
These reactions are inevitable, my Beys.

445
01:04:57,178 --> 01:05:03,208
We don't doubt the road we're
headed towards.

446
01:05:06,709 --> 01:05:12,989
Saltuk! Hand the remaining gold out to
other Beys.

447
01:08:05,862 --> 01:08:07,442
Open!

448
01:08:13,651 --> 01:08:15,818
Approach, Selcan Hatun.

449
01:08:15,818 --> 01:08:19,348
Do you want me to crawl or walk,
Dündar Bey?

450
01:08:19,409 --> 01:08:23,555
Because, you've been a dog of Mongols.
Your traditions may have changed.

451
01:08:23,555 --> 01:08:27,325
Watch your mouth, Selcan Hatun!

452
01:08:27,456 --> 01:08:32,186
I watch my mouth according to
my traditions, Dündar Bey.

453
01:08:32,297 --> 01:08:38,107
Hatun, man things, politics, are beyond
your ken.

454
01:08:38,107 --> 01:08:41,210
Mind your own business, let me not
break your heart.

455
01:08:41,210 --> 01:08:46,310
Oh hey, look at Sheik Süleyman Shah's
son Dündar Bey.

456
01:08:46,320 --> 01:08:50,960
Look what this Bey says. He was supposed
to honor Kayı Tribe.

457
01:08:51,237 --> 01:08:55,847
What my Osman should do now?
You've been a slave for Mongols.

458
01:08:55,972 --> 01:08:59,020
Who can stop Osman now?
From now on...

459
01:08:59,020 --> 01:09:02,960
From now on, whatever I say is law.

460
01:09:04,703 --> 01:09:07,173
Osman is the one who brought us here.

461
01:09:07,233 --> 01:09:13,353
Should I have let Mongols
destroy our tribe?

462
01:09:13,732 --> 01:09:15,884
You are talking about the glory of Kayı.

463
01:09:15,884 --> 01:09:20,424
I didn't pay attention to that, I had to
protect us.

464
01:09:20,931 --> 01:09:24,401
Kayı is the banner lord of this country
now.

465
01:09:24,585 --> 01:09:28,335
Don't talk any more.
Or you'll be exiled.

466
01:09:28,408 --> 01:09:30,868
Pull yourself together.

467
01:09:30,881 --> 01:09:33,241
Enough, Dündar Bey.

468
01:09:33,398 --> 01:09:35,318
Stop.

469
01:09:36,644 --> 01:09:38,694
You're arguing with everyone.

470
01:09:38,965 --> 01:09:43,615
First Osman, then Batur, now Selcan Hatun.

471
01:09:44,813 --> 01:09:50,453
This Hatun is traditional. She cares about
the tribe. What do you mean by exile?

472
01:09:51,937 --> 01:09:54,997
My Batur followed Osman's path.

473
01:09:55,741 --> 01:10:01,621
If Selcan Hatun goes, I and my daughter
will go with her, too.

474
01:10:33,684 --> 01:10:37,524
This is a blessed day.

475
01:10:43,485 --> 01:10:48,165
This is a great, blessed day, Kongar!

476
01:11:54,313 --> 01:11:57,143
What do you want from us, Balgay?

477
01:11:57,886 --> 01:12:00,796
Why are you in hurry to talk with us?

478
01:12:00,874 --> 01:12:05,434
The souls' power has been my armor.

479
01:12:07,220 --> 01:12:12,730
Cengiz Han's mouth has become mine,
so has his sword.

480
01:12:15,072 --> 01:12:20,782
The power in my blood comes from Cengiz
Han's laws.

481
01:12:21,449 --> 01:12:23,549
You should know that.

482
01:13:31,713 --> 01:13:33,593
Bring the chest!

483
01:13:37,716 --> 01:13:39,836
My Batur Bey...

484
01:13:39,855 --> 01:13:41,717
Be ready.

485
01:13:41,717 --> 01:13:45,707
We will not go without a kill for sure,
my Konur.

486
01:13:57,427 --> 01:13:59,257
Who are you?

487
01:14:02,074 --> 01:14:04,184
I asked who you are!

488
01:14:08,562 --> 01:14:11,832
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son Osman.

489
01:14:37,658 --> 01:14:41,078
My Bey, they are coming to take the chest.

490
01:15:02,360 --> 01:15:06,470
My Bey, they are waiting for the chest.

491
01:15:06,910 --> 01:15:11,700
They'd better wait.
Be ready for the battle.

492
01:15:12,531 --> 01:15:14,451
Come on.

493
01:16:19,141 --> 01:16:24,051
Cengiz Han's power is with me.

494
01:16:35,144 --> 01:16:39,744
Geyhatun's brave Commanders.

495
01:16:40,573 --> 01:16:45,244
The laws that carry Cengiz Han's soul...

496
01:16:45,244 --> 01:16:51,034
are in Balgay's blessed hand.
May the souls witness.

497
01:16:51,267 --> 01:16:57,047
May they be my friend.

498
01:16:58,068 --> 01:17:04,063
Today, we obey the laws' power.

499
01:17:04,063 --> 01:17:06,767
Do you hear what you are saying, Balgay?

500
01:17:06,767 --> 01:17:11,707
This power can only belong to
Cengiz Han's grandchildren.

501
01:17:11,929 --> 01:17:14,209
Not in your hand!

502
01:17:15,554 --> 01:17:20,354
Power is with me, Commander Taloy.

503
01:17:22,075 --> 01:17:24,095
Power...

504
01:17:24,884 --> 01:17:26,834
is with Balgay.

505
01:17:28,815 --> 01:17:36,035
If Balgay is right, he will want us to
obey, or he'll kill us.

506
01:17:50,040 --> 01:17:52,670
The chest is empty, Balgay.

507
01:17:57,595 --> 01:18:01,995
Betrayal.

508
01:18:02,930 --> 01:18:06,740
Are you playing with us?

509
01:18:13,737 --> 01:18:16,857
Balgay! What do you think you are doing?

510
01:18:18,692 --> 01:18:23,758
You won't go anywhere until we find
Cengiz Han's laws.

511
01:18:23,758 --> 01:18:27,998
Search everywhere!
Close the entrances and exits.

512
01:18:28,013 --> 01:18:31,773
Search everywhere!

513
01:18:52,400 --> 01:18:54,350
We are going.

514
01:18:59,943 --> 01:19:02,163
Kneel!

515
01:19:21,237 --> 01:19:23,337
Search everywhere!

516
01:21:07,527 --> 01:21:10,097
Come on, Alps!

517
01:21:23,370 --> 01:21:27,350
There are dead Alps in the
back of the tribe. They ran from there.

518
01:21:27,350 --> 01:21:29,027
Kungar is following them.

519
01:21:29,027 --> 01:21:33,897
This must be Osman.

520
01:21:35,634 --> 01:21:38,574
Search everywhere, Cerkutay!

521
01:21:57,717 --> 01:22:03,267
I swear on my ancestor Cengiz's soul...

522
01:22:06,518 --> 01:22:11,928
I will tear Osman's flesh apart his bones.

523
01:22:14,068 --> 01:22:20,118
I will drink his blood and prepare a
feast from his flesh!

524
01:22:29,366 --> 01:22:31,886
I know you are ambitious.

525
01:22:32,482 --> 01:22:34,319
You loved the power.

526
01:22:34,319 --> 01:22:36,422
But I didn't expect this.

527
01:22:36,422 --> 01:22:40,992
One should be prepared for what he
doesn't expect, Hatun.

528
01:22:41,726 --> 01:22:43,786
You bothered me so much.

529
01:22:43,861 --> 01:22:49,451
Now, you wonder what will
happen to you and you are worried.

530
01:22:49,683 --> 01:22:52,903
Am I your new enemy?

531
01:22:54,638 --> 01:22:58,998
No, you have gone mad.

532
01:22:59,074 --> 01:23:03,134
Didn't you say that "In Kayı, everyone
has power..."

533
01:23:03,134 --> 01:23:09,034
but only you have both power and wisdom."
Ha?

534
01:23:09,466 --> 01:23:15,446
Let this tribe benefit from my wisdom.

535
01:23:15,598 --> 01:23:21,688
You couldn't be a father to your son.
Are you talking about being a Bey?

536
01:23:22,519 --> 01:23:25,039
I'd laugh, Dündar Bey.

537
01:23:26,882 --> 01:23:31,702
You've been talking about Beylik (Beyship)
and power for years.

538
01:23:31,801 --> 01:23:36,761
Here is the Bey, here is the power!

539
01:23:37,733 --> 01:23:42,833
If you don't like, the door is open.
I've had enough!

540
01:23:55,975 --> 01:24:00,155
Lucky you.
You have protected the entrustment.

541
01:24:00,313 --> 01:24:02,783
You have deflated the enemy.

542
01:24:02,819 --> 01:24:05,319
Thank my Allah, my Sheik.

543
01:24:06,764 --> 01:24:14,204
This life, this world, this body,
this greenery

544
01:24:14,347 --> 01:24:16,803
all are entrusted to humans.

545
01:24:16,803 --> 01:24:21,186
So, a human must be Al-Emin (trustworthy)

546
01:24:21,186 --> 01:24:25,796
He must protect the entrustments.

547
01:24:26,143 --> 01:24:29,253
How can we do it, my Sheik?

548
01:24:30,908 --> 01:24:34,478
By being a human.

549
01:24:35,905 --> 01:24:38,212
Aren't we humans already?

550
01:24:38,212 --> 01:24:40,702
Physically, yes.

551
01:24:41,131 --> 01:24:43,421
What about mentally?

552
01:24:43,725 --> 01:24:45,702
What about spiritually?

553
01:24:45,702 --> 01:24:48,132
What about in your heart?

554
01:24:50,242 --> 01:24:53,152
We came to this world as humans.

555
01:24:53,892 --> 01:24:59,032
Are we going to go to the hereafter
as humans, Osman Bey?

556
01:25:00,525 --> 01:25:06,175
Just like there is a way to go
somewhere...

557
01:25:06,482 --> 01:25:10,212
Just like science has its own way...

558
01:25:10,317 --> 01:25:16,907
There is a way to go to hereafter
as a human, for sure.

559
01:25:16,968 --> 01:25:19,388
What is that way, my Sheik?

560
01:25:20,178 --> 01:25:23,758
Protecting the entrustment, son.

561
01:25:25,554 --> 01:25:29,964
Firstly, we will clear our hearts.

562
01:25:29,986 --> 01:25:34,786
Because, a sacred hadith says...

563
01:25:34,946 --> 01:25:42,886
" I couldn't take place in the whole world
but, I could take place in a Muslim heart.

564
01:25:44,596 --> 01:25:47,965
We will be wise, son.

565
01:25:47,965 --> 01:25:51,605
We are not going to be interested in
bubbling.

566
01:25:51,868 --> 01:25:56,938
We are always going to think of
good deeds.

567
01:25:57,646 --> 01:26:03,336
We will protect the world, and make the
universe prosperous.

568
01:26:03,518 --> 01:26:12,368
While doing something, we are going to
calculate everything, and not hurt anyone.

569
01:26:12,875 --> 01:26:15,545
We are not going to deform the world.

570
01:26:16,175 --> 01:26:18,995
We are not going to hurt the animals.

571
01:26:18,999 --> 01:26:24,319
We are not going to turn nature into
a human trash.

572
01:26:25,184 --> 01:26:30,694
We are an Al-Emin (trustworthy) Prophet's
community.

573
01:26:30,774 --> 01:26:36,018
We have to be Al-Emin (trustworthy) in
every place we take.

574
01:26:36,168 --> 01:26:44,338
In family, in government works,
in commerce, in agriculture.

575
01:26:44,474 --> 01:26:49,114
We are not going to lose
this characteristic.

576
01:26:49,336 --> 01:26:54,326
Because, if we can't our Allah's
entrustment...

577
01:26:54,619 --> 01:26:59,369
we will be disgraced.

578
01:26:59,801 --> 01:27:06,021
The ones who protect the entrustment
will decide the fate of the future.

579
01:27:06,310 --> 01:27:12,070
Al-Emins ( Trustworthy ones) will
resurrect this state.

580
01:27:13,378 --> 01:27:18,678
Allah is with Al-Emins
(Trustworthy ones).

581
01:27:46,404 --> 01:27:48,174
Stop!

582
01:27:49,885 --> 01:27:53,798
I said stop! What are you doing?
Give it to me!

583
01:27:55,748 --> 01:27:58,548
What do you think you are doing, heh?

584
01:27:59,849 --> 01:28:06,621
Won't you be ashamed against Ertuğrul Bey?
Are you ignoring the tradition of Kayı?

585
01:28:06,621 --> 01:28:10,240
It's Dündar Bey's order, Selcan Hatun.
Let it be.

586
01:28:10,240 --> 01:28:15,580
Damn your manhood.
Damn your courage.

587
01:28:16,376 --> 01:28:23,346
Saltuğ. Didn't your father grow up with
my Sheik Süleyman?

588
01:28:23,595 --> 01:28:25,045
Ha?

589
01:28:25,122 --> 01:28:27,062
What about you?

590
01:28:27,076 --> 01:28:32,306
Didn't your father become a martyr while
fighting for Ertuğrul Bey?

591
01:28:32,570 --> 01:28:38,730
No! I will not let you loot my Ertuğrul
Bey's tent!

592
01:28:39,747 --> 01:28:44,687
Don't, Selcan Hatun.
Talk to the Bey.

593
01:29:18,976 --> 01:29:21,616
I can't believe this.

594
01:29:24,529 --> 01:29:28,059
There is no Bey to hear me out.

595
01:29:28,842 --> 01:29:32,002
I wish I was blind and not see this.

596
01:29:33,189 --> 01:29:36,679
Protect us, my Allah.

597
01:30:01,778 --> 01:30:05,992
Go to Cerkutay immediately. Selcan Hatun
is out of the tribe.

598
01:30:05,992 --> 01:30:08,592
Where she is going is obvious.

599
01:30:25,868 --> 01:30:27,738
My Bala...

600
01:30:28,748 --> 01:30:31,307
I want to come with you.

601
01:30:31,307 --> 01:30:34,527
I don't want you to go alone.

602
01:30:35,594 --> 01:30:42,624
Don't worry, it won't take long.
I will see Selcan Hatun, talk a bit.

603
01:30:59,324 --> 01:31:02,704
Selcan Hatun knows Osman the best,
Gonca Hatun.

604
01:31:04,103 --> 01:31:09,223
I want to freshen up.
She will show me the way.

605
01:31:51,003 --> 01:31:53,943
You still don't look at my face.

606
01:31:54,493 --> 01:31:57,483
I was mistaken about you, Osman Bey.

607
01:31:57,564 --> 01:32:00,044
I don't want to push you.

608
01:32:01,837 --> 01:32:05,557
I will tell the truth again, maybe
you couldn't understand me.

609
01:32:06,959 --> 01:32:09,839
My accompany needs to...

610
01:32:09,839 --> 01:32:15,229
know where to be deaf, and where to be
a bow.

611
01:32:16,814 --> 01:32:22,564
However, if you suspect, it's hard
of course.

612
01:32:29,862 --> 01:32:34,732
I am not the one who suspects, it's you,
Osman Bey.

613
01:32:40,641 --> 01:32:44,051
Obviously, we are getting nowhere.

614
01:32:45,374 --> 01:32:51,454
I can't talk with someone who can't
hear what she is saying.

615
01:33:41,868 --> 01:33:45,798
I brought the Nökers who were responsible
of the guards.

616
01:34:24,503 --> 01:34:31,323
While my ancestor Cengiz's blessed
entrustment were being stolen...

617
01:34:33,401 --> 01:34:38,091
didn't those ears hear anything?

618
01:34:50,028 --> 01:34:56,548
The ear, which doesn't hear the enemy,
is useless!

619
01:35:10,588 --> 01:35:15,428
Eyes, which doesn't see the enemy...

620
01:35:23,231 --> 01:35:27,781
Useless eyes!

621
01:35:48,508 --> 01:35:53,578
The Nöker who doesn't have the Mongol
nobility...

622
01:35:53,625 --> 01:35:58,085
will be blind, will be deaf!

623
01:36:06,868 --> 01:36:09,368
Burn them.

624
01:36:09,837 --> 01:36:17,817
May the wolves and birds not be poisoned
with their useless flesh.

625
01:36:33,879 --> 01:36:35,779
Did they manage to escape?

626
01:36:42,675 --> 01:36:46,028
Wherever he goes, we will
find Osman, Balgay.

627
01:36:46,028 --> 01:36:51,378
I don't need fancy words.
I want blood!

628
01:36:51,661 --> 01:36:57,891
Like a flood, I want blood, Cerkutay!

629
01:36:58,935 --> 01:37:03,745
Commander Balgay, the other Kayı tribe's
Bey Samsa...

630
01:37:03,965 --> 01:37:08,725
he disagreed with Osman.
Our man in the tribe said.

631
01:37:18,265 --> 01:37:22,595
An arrow to hunt an eagle...

632
01:37:24,397 --> 01:37:27,917
is made of eagle's feathers.

633
01:37:29,250 --> 01:37:36,260
Kongar, sacrifice a man of yours.
Send him to Samsa's tribe.

634
01:37:36,727 --> 01:37:41,367
- And bring him to you?
- He will not come.

635
01:37:41,483 --> 01:37:48,003
Now, what we need is Samsa's courage.

636
01:37:48,056 --> 01:37:53,136
The man you send should play with
his pride so that...

637
01:37:53,489 --> 01:37:57,049
Samsa kills him.

638
01:37:58,227 --> 01:38:03,847
When he killed a couple of Mongols..

639
01:38:04,431 --> 01:38:08,223
Freedom lover Kayıs will be gathered
around him.

640
01:38:08,223 --> 01:38:14,243
At that exact time, with Osman's
ambition...

641
01:38:15,366 --> 01:38:19,046
Samsa's courage will fight.

642
01:38:19,048 --> 01:38:23,998
And we won't tire ourselves.

643
01:38:34,647 --> 01:38:37,377
Put it properly, Alps!

644
01:39:37,136 --> 01:39:39,136
My Father.

645
01:39:39,831 --> 01:39:45,431
I will carry your entrustment with honor.

646
01:40:09,108 --> 01:40:16,538
Shepherd, shepherd, if you die, who will
take care of these goats, shepherd?

647
01:40:17,024 --> 01:40:21,184
Don't think I am a quiet sheep.

648
01:40:22,182 --> 01:40:26,212
I swear on my father Süleyman Shah.

649
01:40:26,320 --> 01:40:30,880
I will pay you off for what you've done,
Balgay.

650
01:40:32,539 --> 01:40:34,679
I will.

651
01:41:02,200 --> 01:41:08,387
Ignoble Balgay must have gone mad when
he found out that he lost the chest.

652
01:41:11,667 --> 01:41:14,307
Balgay is the enemy we know, brother.

653
01:41:15,076 --> 01:41:17,486
What about the factious' in us?

654
01:41:20,552 --> 01:41:25,452
A community can't get rid of the enemies...

655
01:41:25,779 --> 01:41:28,689
as long as they don't take care of the
factious'.

656
01:41:29,833 --> 01:41:33,523
If someone becomes a factious...

657
01:41:33,564 --> 01:41:36,644
he must be killed.

658
01:41:37,883 --> 01:41:40,283
We will take care of them one by one.

659
01:41:40,891 --> 01:41:43,521
We will tear their lungs apart!

660
01:41:54,497 --> 01:41:56,447
Sons!

661
01:41:58,949 --> 01:42:00,739
What's the problem, Bamsi Bey?

662
01:42:00,812 --> 01:42:04,342
Dündar became flag officer of...

663
01:42:04,793 --> 01:42:08,613
...Balgay, Osman.

664
01:42:14,546 --> 01:42:16,716
What are you saying, Bamsi Bey!

665
01:42:18,578 --> 01:42:22,518
Balgay declared him as a flag officer
in exchange for his obedience.

666
01:42:26,907 --> 01:42:30,377
As a first duty, he displayed a flag of...

667
01:42:30,607 --> 01:42:34,167
...flag officer near to our honourable
flag.

668
01:42:35,200 --> 01:42:36,490
Father!

669
01:42:37,158 --> 01:42:38,608
You shouldn't have done this.

670
01:42:38,891 --> 01:42:41,381
Even Alisar wouldn't do such a thing.

671
01:42:48,161 --> 01:42:49,781
Either freedom...

672
01:42:50,366 --> 01:42:51,196
...or death.

673
01:42:54,762 --> 01:42:56,862
Those who rebel control the chair...

674
01:42:57,160 --> 01:42:58,810
...not those who obey.

675
01:43:00,302 --> 01:43:02,262
Don't fall into error, guys.

676
01:43:03,894 --> 01:43:05,874
Firstly, We'll solve these affairs.

677
01:43:06,057 --> 01:43:08,567
Then we'll fall down the Tent.

678
01:43:11,766 --> 01:43:14,806
We'll tear off that flag officer flag.

679
01:43:15,198 --> 01:43:15,918
Move!

680
01:43:16,758 --> 01:43:18,068
You go!

681
01:43:18,350 --> 01:43:19,640
I'll come.

682
01:44:03,632 --> 01:44:04,562
Come here.

683
01:44:10,650 --> 01:44:11,630
Ya Allah.

684
01:44:30,890 --> 01:44:31,660
Salvador.

685
01:44:32,971 --> 01:44:34,231
Freak!

686
01:44:51,062 --> 01:44:52,092
Don't struggle.

687
01:44:53,433 --> 01:44:54,403
Leave him to me.

688
01:44:56,800 --> 01:44:57,600
Leave.

689
01:45:04,088 --> 01:45:05,188
Walk up!

690
01:45:07,239 --> 01:45:08,389
I didn't betray.

691
01:45:10,299 --> 01:45:11,549
I didn't betray.

692
01:45:21,152 --> 01:45:23,202
Eshedu en la ilahe ilallah...

693
01:45:24,511 --> 01:45:27,331
...ve eshedu ennemu muhammeden
abduhu ve resulu.

694
01:45:29,054 --> 01:45:30,384
Liar factious.

695
01:45:30,516 --> 01:45:31,716
You can't.

696
01:45:31,978 --> 01:45:34,818
You can't go anywhere
this time.

697
01:45:37,467 --> 01:45:38,377
You can't again.

698
01:45:38,383 --> 01:45:39,343
Bamsi Bey.

699
01:45:39,834 --> 01:45:40,814
Don't do it.

700
01:45:41,568 --> 01:45:43,188
Listen to me, Bamsi Bey.

701
01:45:47,735 --> 01:45:49,995
You leave him for me, Bamsi Bey.

702
01:45:51,025 --> 01:45:52,465
Let Sıddık go!

703
01:45:58,530 --> 01:45:59,440
Dont do it, my Bey.

704
01:45:59,688 --> 01:46:01,418
I'm not gonna say it again.

705
01:46:07,310 --> 01:46:08,620
Arghhh!

706
01:46:11,058 --> 01:46:12,968
He is not Sıddık.

707
01:46:13,140 --> 01:46:14,670
He is Salvador.

708
01:46:14,829 --> 01:46:15,639
Salvador.

709
01:46:27,029 --> 01:46:28,239
Are you okay?

710
01:46:30,431 --> 01:46:31,671
Yes, Osman Bey.

711
01:46:36,240 --> 01:46:38,350
They know nothing about it.

712
01:46:39,094 --> 01:46:40,214
Sorry.

713
01:46:41,094 --> 01:46:42,634
No problem, Osman Bey.

714
01:46:52,958 --> 01:46:54,498
Is there any news?

715
01:46:54,973 --> 01:46:57,003
Everything is going as planned

716
01:46:57,363 --> 01:47:00,673
Sofia will request Balgay to trap you.

717
01:47:05,539 --> 01:47:06,489
Osman.

718
01:47:07,893 --> 01:47:09,943
Is he really Sıddık?

719
01:47:15,139 --> 01:47:17,619
I promised something to you, Bamsi Bey.

720
01:47:18,342 --> 01:47:21,072
I will be loyal to my promise
until I am dead.

721
01:47:55,967 --> 01:47:57,337
If they play with us...

722
01:47:57,902 --> 01:47:59,032
...we'll, too.

723
01:48:00,110 --> 01:48:02,800
As long as we continue to struggle.

724
01:48:09,242 --> 01:48:12,742
I see the reflection of Ertugrul Bey
through your eyes.

725
01:48:13,971 --> 01:48:15,281
He is such a man that...

726
01:48:16,288 --> 01:48:18,948
...he sees back of the mountains.

727
01:48:19,192 --> 01:48:20,882
He is such a man that...

728
01:48:21,060 --> 01:48:23,360
...he lights a fire behind the fog.

729
01:48:23,698 --> 01:48:25,218
Well done, brave man!

730
01:48:26,287 --> 01:48:27,597
Well done.

731
01:48:29,364 --> 01:48:31,144
Masha Allah (praise be), my Bey.

732
01:48:31,386 --> 01:48:33,036
Long live with your intelligence.

733
01:48:33,066 --> 01:48:33,936
Well done.

734
01:48:33,936 --> 01:48:34,923
Mashallah.

735
01:48:35,282 --> 01:48:37,672
Now, I will go to give the entrustment

736
01:48:37,867 --> 01:48:39,537
Be ready when I come.

737
01:48:40,700 --> 01:48:42,560
We will fall down the Tent.

738
01:48:44,344 --> 01:48:45,634
Let's do it, Osman.

739
01:49:29,286 --> 01:49:31,856
You couldn't guess the right time, woman.

740
01:49:33,587 --> 01:49:35,517
While Balgay is blood-thirsty...

741
01:49:36,136 --> 01:49:38,076
...you appear before him.

742
01:49:44,163 --> 01:49:47,503
In contrast, there couldn't
be better time to meet than now...

743
01:49:49,179 --> 01:49:52,619
...great commander Balgay.

744
01:49:53,099 --> 01:49:54,319
I heard that...

745
01:49:54,954 --> 01:49:57,124
...Osman took what he had given.

746
01:49:58,006 --> 01:49:59,656
From where did you hear?

747
01:49:59,714 --> 01:50:02,224
You came from away.

748
01:50:03,131 --> 01:50:07,131
We've been here for 1000 years.

749
01:50:10,381 --> 01:50:14,381
Did you eventually
learn why I hate Osman that much?

750
01:50:18,584 --> 01:50:20,584
He is a rabid dog.

751
01:50:21,632 --> 01:50:23,442
He is a troubler.

752
01:50:25,196 --> 01:50:26,796
If you listen to me...

753
01:50:27,716 --> 01:50:30,106
...you'll have the road
which goes to hunting.

754
01:50:41,197 --> 01:50:42,147
How?

755
01:50:43,697 --> 01:50:47,697
Osman has someone who he trusts so much.

756
01:50:49,703 --> 01:50:51,803
And he serves to me.

757
01:50:59,881 --> 01:51:02,691
You're sneaky as a marten.

758
01:51:02,731 --> 01:51:06,731
and smart as a fox.

759
01:51:07,767 --> 01:51:11,767
What do you want in return?

760
01:51:12,222 --> 01:51:14,922
You will understand, Balgay.

761
01:51:16,613 --> 01:51:19,213
We'll speak calmly.

762
01:51:54,449 --> 01:51:56,969
By the name of 99 names of great Allah...

763
01:51:57,389 --> 01:52:01,635
...who fills our heart with faith and
makes whatever he wants happen.

764
01:52:03,965 --> 01:52:06,255
The nobles of my Tent.

765
01:52:06,650 --> 01:52:08,220
Ghazi Beys.

766
01:52:09,853 --> 01:52:11,513
The Kayı fell from grace...

767
01:52:11,649 --> 01:52:14,659
...because of Dundar's improper
behaviours.

768
01:52:15,902 --> 01:52:19,902
While he took the chair of Ertugrul
Bey thanks to Mongol,

769
01:52:20,874 --> 01:52:24,144
he brought flag of Mongol and planted
it to the Kayı Oba.

770
01:52:24,630 --> 01:52:26,400
From now on, we have hope.

771
01:52:26,604 --> 01:52:27,894
Soon...

772
01:52:28,018 --> 01:52:29,778
...mongols will bother our Tent.

773
01:52:29,817 --> 01:52:31,697
We are few in number, my Bey.

774
01:52:31,958 --> 01:52:32,978
We can't resist.

775
01:52:33,029 --> 01:52:36,209
There must be a miracle to defeat them.

776
01:52:36,356 --> 01:52:40,606
Do we need to wait for swift birds to battle
with tyrants who occupy Muslim homelands.

777
01:52:43,639 --> 01:52:47,979
Those swift birds will throw stones at us
first if we don't rebel.

778
01:52:51,199 --> 01:52:53,289
Don't we have a time...

779
01:52:53,822 --> 01:52:56,072
...of death after all?

780
01:52:56,984 --> 01:53:00,424
Now that death comes just 1 time,
I am asking you...

781
01:53:01,249 --> 01:53:05,249
...why shouldn't it come for	martyrdom?

782
01:53:05,801 --> 01:53:07,921
I hope nothing's wrong, inshallah.

783
01:53:10,288 --> 01:53:11,408
My bey.

784
01:53:11,478 --> 01:53:12,898
Mongols...

785
01:53:22,378 --> 01:53:24,148
If I came here for war...

786
01:53:24,234 --> 01:53:26,384
...I wouldn't come like that.

787
01:53:27,524 --> 01:53:29,194
My visiting is friendly.

788
01:53:34,811 --> 01:53:37,521
We don't have any friendship with the
tyranny.

789
01:53:37,681 --> 01:53:40,531
Our rage is with those who don't obey us.

790
01:53:40,581 --> 01:53:44,581
What've we done to your Tent?

791
01:53:44,708 --> 01:53:46,588
Tell me why you came here.

792
01:53:46,642 --> 01:53:49,712
Commander Balgay wants you in his marquee
in Kartalkaynı.

793
01:53:49,774 --> 01:53:51,374
What does he want from me?

794
01:53:51,454 --> 01:53:53,694
Balgay doesn't request, he just takes.

795
01:53:54,339 --> 01:53:58,339
If you come, it will be beneficial to
the Tent.

796
01:54:06,367 --> 01:54:07,837
What if I don't?

797
01:54:07,879 --> 01:54:11,879
This time you can't rescue just
by being pack animal, Samsa.

798
01:54:14,773 --> 01:54:16,703
Balgay will be your butcher.

799
01:54:16,976 --> 01:54:20,976
We'll show around your head in
all Oba as a deterrent.

800
01:54:41,775 --> 01:54:43,745
Announce it to all the Tents...

801
01:54:44,899 --> 01:54:47,329
...Samsa Bey started the fire of freedom.

802
01:54:47,347 --> 01:54:48,557
All right, my Bey!

803
01:56:24,704 --> 01:56:26,644
Betrayal.

804
01:56:30,948 --> 01:56:33,318
Betrayal!

805
01:56:33,963 --> 01:56:34,833
Betrayal!

806
01:56:41,031 --> 01:56:42,881
Betrayal!

807
01:56:43,118 --> 01:56:45,888
Betrayal!

808
01:57:44,872 --> 01:57:47,252
I've done my duty unconditionally.

809
01:57:47,461 --> 01:57:48,371
Bey father.

810
01:58:51,119 --> 01:58:54,839
I'm proud of you always.

811
01:58:55,091 --> 01:58:59,091
But, you honoured me this time.

812
01:59:02,392 --> 01:59:06,392
I can do everything for you, Bey father.

813
01:59:09,868 --> 01:59:12,608
May your banner lordship and Kayı Beyship
be everlasting

814
01:59:12,619 --> 01:59:15,389
May Allah don't make you away from us.

815
01:59:20,635 --> 01:59:21,455
Osman

816
01:59:21,877 --> 01:59:25,217
He'll learn what you've done
sooner or later.

817
01:59:25,383 --> 01:59:26,083
I know.

818
01:59:28,145 --> 01:59:29,635
He'll pursue you.

819
01:59:30,921 --> 01:59:32,781
I'll be cautious this time.

820
01:59:33,107 --> 01:59:36,177
The pain of the dagger that
he stabbed to my chest has relieved.

821
01:59:36,330 --> 01:59:37,370
But...

822
01:59:37,600 --> 01:59:39,930
It's rage is still alive
inside my body.

823
01:59:40,719 --> 01:59:42,519
May Allah protect us.

824
01:59:55,927 --> 01:59:57,007
My son.

825
01:59:59,510 --> 02:00:00,430
My Batur.

826
02:00:00,706 --> 02:00:01,476
Mother.

827
02:00:05,325 --> 02:00:07,265
My son.

828
02:00:13,290 --> 02:00:16,810
I brought your son to you.

829
02:00:17,475 --> 02:00:21,335
Don't mess with my decisions again.

830
02:00:27,153 --> 02:00:29,673
You are the hope of the Kayı, Dundar Bey.

831
02:00:30,766 --> 02:00:35,056
If I make you sad because of my
mother instincts...

832
02:00:35,549 --> 02:00:37,249
...forgive me.

833
02:00:38,476 --> 02:00:40,706
May your banner lordship be everlasting.

834
02:01:15,663 --> 02:01:17,763
Is there any problem, my Bey?

835
02:01:19,961 --> 02:01:20,731
Betrayal.

836
02:01:22,188 --> 02:01:24,108
Betrayal!

837
02:01:27,901 --> 02:01:29,971
What did Batur say, Aykut?

838
02:01:30,125 --> 02:01:32,645
He said I would go to
hunting and went out, my Bey.

839
02:01:33,676 --> 02:01:37,546
We've everything in here. Why would
he go to hunting in this situation?

840
02:01:37,643 --> 02:01:39,863
Old habits die hard.

841
02:01:43,965 --> 02:01:45,455
To where, my Bey?

842
02:01:46,033 --> 02:01:48,143
To take the life of Batur.

843
02:01:56,219 --> 02:01:58,719
Do you think it can continue like that,
Selcan Hatun?

844
02:01:58,759 --> 02:02:01,867
I say I can do everything for you.
He says It's secret.

845
02:02:02,777 --> 02:02:05,017
Is there a secret to loving heart?

846
02:02:07,688 --> 02:02:10,768
Look. You are silent.

847
02:02:12,416 --> 02:02:13,986
There is nothing to say.

848
02:02:14,190 --> 02:02:16,390
Now that Osman doesn't trust me...

849
02:02:16,507 --> 02:02:19,257
...he doesn't need my companionship
as well.

850
02:02:19,620 --> 02:02:21,260
He said that already.

851
02:02:22,302 --> 02:02:24,042
We came to a dead end.

852
02:02:26,056 --> 02:02:28,546
You came to a dead end, huh?

853
02:02:30,384 --> 02:02:31,904
I know him.

854
02:02:32,042 --> 02:02:34,392
It seems he is angry with you.

855
02:02:37,925 --> 02:02:41,525
I thought he loved me so much.

856
02:02:42,878 --> 02:02:46,878
But now I understand that
he doesn't love me anymore.

857
02:02:48,102 --> 02:02:49,482
Look at me.

858
02:02:49,617 --> 02:02:53,617
Being one and bear others and
bearing each other are not the same thing.

859
02:02:55,011 --> 02:02:56,891
You'll learn it later.

860
02:02:58,142 --> 02:03:02,142
Burden of love is the same
for both sides.

861
02:03:03,277 --> 02:03:06,587
It's all about having a heart that can
bear this burden.

862
02:03:06,887 --> 02:03:09,327
My Osman surely loves you.

863
02:03:09,623 --> 02:03:13,183
But he has the blood
of Oguz in his vessels.

864
02:03:24,508 --> 02:03:28,508
His grandfather and father
fell in love, too.

865
02:03:28,539 --> 02:03:30,789
But they said first Tent and traditions
came.

866
02:03:32,365 --> 02:03:34,105
Their wives were the same.

867
02:03:34,265 --> 02:03:37,505
Halime mother didn't ask so many things
to Suleyman.

868
02:03:37,613 --> 02:03:43,123
Without knowing the reason, Halime Sultan
said "okay" to Ertugrul Bey nearly always.

869
02:03:45,699 --> 02:03:48,169
Being wife means being silent and...

870
02:03:48,879 --> 02:03:50,869
...accepting some things.

871
02:03:51,357 --> 02:03:55,357
Otherwise, this love will come to an end.

872
02:03:56,164 --> 02:03:58,794
So you're saying that you've
done something wrong.

873
02:03:58,914 --> 02:04:01,404
You're saying that you broke
Osman's heart in vain.

874
02:04:03,795 --> 02:04:06,655
I'm saying that as long as there
is not treachery in love...

875
02:04:06,655 --> 02:04:08,305
...there isn't dead end.

876
02:04:09,436 --> 02:04:11,496
Maybe Osman is broken.

877
02:04:12,138 --> 02:04:14,018
But if you want to please him...

878
02:04:14,417 --> 02:04:16,497
...he is already your love.

879
02:04:18,619 --> 02:04:21,589
I thought he wouldn't
believe and trust me.

880
02:04:22,787 --> 02:04:25,537
His passion makes me so happy.

881
02:04:25,861 --> 02:04:29,051
But if he doesn't accept me,
I will fall down.

882
02:04:29,119 --> 02:04:30,339
Look at me, my daughter.

883
02:04:31,016 --> 02:04:33,616
Hold on to this love tightly.

884
02:04:34,999 --> 02:04:38,999
Osman won't allow you to fall down
as long as he doesn't.

885
02:04:39,543 --> 02:04:40,863
Don't worry.

886
02:04:52,103 --> 02:04:53,653
Take this to Batur.

887
02:04:53,787 --> 02:04:55,057
His mother sent it.

888
02:05:00,136 --> 02:05:02,316
It's mother's love, my daughter.

889
02:05:02,556 --> 02:05:04,586
Mother worries about her son.

890
02:05:04,706 --> 02:05:06,146
Make it happen.

891
02:05:09,143 --> 02:05:10,453
All the best!

892
02:05:10,781 --> 02:05:12,261
Thanks, Selcan Hatun.

893
02:05:22,299 --> 02:05:23,279
Be ready

894
02:05:23,969 --> 02:05:25,569
We'll pursue the girl.

895
02:05:27,068 --> 02:05:29,768
She'll take us to Osman.

896
02:05:32,802 --> 02:05:33,812
Come on!

897
02:05:33,909 --> 02:05:34,669
Come on!

898
02:05:53,132 --> 02:05:54,012
Come on.

899
02:05:59,666 --> 02:06:01,506
May Allah protect us.

900
02:06:43,014 --> 02:06:44,694
Our road will divide in here.

901
02:06:45,240 --> 02:06:47,720
Take whoever follows us away.

902
02:06:47,818 --> 02:06:48,998
Come on!

903
02:07:11,070 --> 02:07:11,860
Catch her.

904
02:07:19,083 --> 02:07:20,433
Come.

905
02:07:22,064 --> 02:07:24,844
You're all gathered just because of
the fear of one woman.

906
02:07:24,844 --> 02:07:26,436
Come then!

907
02:08:32,919 --> 02:08:34,139
Didn't I told you...

908
02:08:35,437 --> 02:08:37,477
...that you wouldn't...

909
02:08:38,167 --> 02:08:39,287
...damage her?

910
02:09:04,531 --> 02:09:06,461
We kept good burden
this winter, my Bey.

911
02:09:06,770 --> 02:09:10,710
The society is being happy about that as
spring comes.

912
02:09:10,887 --> 02:09:13,087
We've deserved it, Saltuk Alp.

913
02:09:13,609 --> 02:09:15,739
We've faced so many difficulties.

914
02:10:35,179 --> 02:10:36,319
Argh!

915
02:10:40,296 --> 02:10:42,626
Batur!

916
02:10:53,978 --> 02:10:56,408
I told you that there's no excuse...

917
02:10:56,798 --> 02:11:00,438
...for villainy and no compensation
for treachery, Batur.

918
02:11:00,698 --> 02:11:04,378
You didn't listen to me.

919
02:11:04,550 --> 02:11:06,550
I trusted you.

920
02:11:07,237 --> 02:11:09,287
I said you "My brother."

921
02:11:09,482 --> 02:11:10,962
What did you do?

922
02:11:11,112 --> 02:11:12,482
You fooled me.

923
02:11:15,437 --> 02:11:19,467
You sold the dignity
of your father and Kayı at once.

924
02:11:23,843 --> 02:11:28,493
As your father betrayed Ertugrul
Bey and broke the laws...

925
02:11:28,708 --> 02:11:31,208
...you broke me, Batur!

926
02:11:33,574 --> 02:11:36,694
You will pay the price!

927
02:11:47,704 --> 02:11:48,694
Osman!

928
02:11:48,884 --> 02:11:49,654
Batur!

929
02:11:49,764 --> 02:11:50,514
Brother!

930
02:11:50,605 --> 02:11:51,625
Don't do it, brother!

931
02:11:51,650 --> 02:11:52,460
Please!

932
02:11:52,510 --> 02:11:53,870
Don't do it, brother!

933
02:12:03,608 --> 02:12:04,318
Osman!

934
02:12:04,352 --> 02:12:05,512
Let me go!

935
02:12:11,588 --> 02:12:12,908
Bastards!

936
02:12:13,257 --> 02:12:14,177
Let me go!

937
02:12:14,231 --> 02:12:15,121
Let me go!

938
02:12:18,152 --> 02:12:19,392
Wait.

939
02:12:31,035 --> 02:12:33,975
Osman!

940
02:13:02,539 --> 02:13:04,779
Batur!

941
02:13:05,349 --> 02:13:30,249
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com